From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:16:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 59/59] arm64: dts: rockchip: h96-max-v58: keep watchdog
 running at power off

BL31 v1.37 accepts the virtual-poweroff IRQ list but wakes on neither
the IR power key nor the RTC alarm, so standby would leave the board
off until replugged. Drop the CRU reset from &wdt: power off ends in a
watchdog restart about 45 s later, as since v6.2. Standby IRQ list kept
for a later BL31.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
index e18193f7f..b068ece8d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-h96-max-v58.dts
@@ -192,9 +192,7 @@ &uart9 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-/* CRU reset makes dw_wdt_stop() a real stop: systemd disarms at poweroff before standby */
 &wdt {
-	resets = <&cru SRST_P_WDT0>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
